<title>UK: BIL sets $200 million four-year bond.</title>
<headline>BIL sets $200 million four-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Banque Internationale a Luxembourg and Citibank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE INTERNATIONALE A LUXEMBOURG</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     6.375     MATURITY    12.MAR.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.25    PAY DATE    12.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.675     REOFFER    99.85     SPREAD	+10.5 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 1-10	SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.40	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED NOV 1999 AND JAN 2002 W/I</p>
<p>			    U.S. TREASURIES</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
